// beside main's statements (test/plan-witness.ts): the status search of the viewer's library, the status search of the
// viewer's own account_id (the author window alone), and the hashtag search's library windows. Each rewrite is main's
// statement with the window pins added and nothing else (main's hashtag statement also kept the space its empty
// mention term left). Under the plan audit's singleton statistics and after ANALYZE, taken once every population
// exists, each returns main's rows and reads no more than main. The viewer's own key (its statuses, boosts, favourites,
// bookmarks and mentions) grows in a world small enough that it dominates the statistics, and so do the same rows of
// the accounts on either side of it; each is counted by its own predicate. Import-shaped rows: one status in several
// sources at once, a silent mention (a recipient the API does not show), and search text with NUL; ids are unique, so
// the order has no ties. Every other statement the flows make is allowed literally; any further statement fails.

